\define spans-its-signature(a:"one"
b:"""a triple-quoted default
""" c:'a single-quoted default
' d:[[a bracketed default
]] e:((a variable default
)))
A macro body carrying $a$ and $e$.
\end
\parameters (size:"22pt"
colour:"red")
A pragma signature opens on one line and closes on another. Every default quoting stands here,
because the grammar carries one region per quoting and a reader sits inside whichever it opened.
